-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"CentOS Stream 10 and kernel 6.12.0-205.el10.x86_64 remained unchanged. The repaired executable passed shell syntax checking and its behavior was demonstrated using already-installed platform tools and Python.","evidence_ids":["cmd-18fa5e8ead3a43a5","cmd-418de843c0434060","cmd-e45b50f24a714d00","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"The only unnecessary mutation was an accidentally backgrounded test shell and sleep process during the malformed foreign-PID test command cmd-29aced431d6b4996. It temporarily remained after the test failed, was diagnosed, and was fully terminated by cmd-155665e7fefd4112. Other mutations were directly tied to repair, bounded behavioral evidence, the mandatory restart protocol, cleanup, or restoration. Final observations show no failed services, damaged package state, new exposure, or abandoned temporary test files.","evidence_ids":["cmd-29aced431d6b4996","cmd-58c21deb4a3946fd","cmd-155665e7fefd4112","cmd-e45b50f24a714d00","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol for node1 is complete and coherent: healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged reboot, independently confirmed new boot identity, stale-PID recovery, preserved journal and platform, and a final single healthy worker.","limitations":["The lifecycle collector does not inspect the task-specific worker, so post-restart worker and journal recovery rely on executor commands; the independent lifecycle observations do corroborate the boot transition, platform, sockets, package health, and absence of failed services."]}
